<title>JAPAN: Foreign investment in Japan mkts in March--JSDA.</title>
<headline>Foreign investment in Japan mkts in March--JSDA.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investment by non-residents in Japanese capital markets for March, region by region and in billions of yen, was as follows, the Japan Securities Dealers' Association (JSDA) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>	   INVESTMENT IN YEN BONDS</p>
<p>	  US/Canada Europe   Asia     Others   Total</p>
<p> March   +368.5   +511.4   +493.5   +257.5   +1,630.9</p>
<p> February+219.6   +863.9   +453.7   +140.8   +1,678.0</p>
<p>	   INVESTMENT IN JAPANESE STOCKS</p>
<p> March   +194.6   +131.1   +42.8    -4.6     +363.9</p>
<p> February+224.6    +178.7   +22.6    +3.2     +429.1</p>
<p>Region refers to the nationality of investors. The section marked &quot;others&quot; includes investors in the Middle East, Latin America, Africa and Oceania, the JSDA said.</p>
<p>Yen bonds are government and corporate debt with maturities of more than one year and include yen-denominated bonds issued in Japan by non-residents (samurai bonds), warrant bonds and bank debentures, but exclude dual-currency bonds and euroyen bonds, the JSDA said.</p>
<p>Figures, given on a delivery basis, may not tally due to rounding.</p>
<p>---Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-5473-3748</p>
</text>
